(ned -- A ZERO DETECTION against the puck, operator spec 2026-08-03)
(MODEL. The rod slides DOWN PAST the puck at a standoff, then drives inward.)
(The puck does NOT need to extend downward: whatever station along the rod's)
(SHAFT happens to be level with the puck is what makes contact, so every)
(depth touches the SAME feature of the puck with a DIFFERENT part of the rod.)
(A vertical rod therefore contacts at the same Y at every depth. A rod tilted)
(by A does not -- the station that reaches the puck sits further off the)
(centreline the deeper the tip goes:)
(     recorded Y = constant - depth x tan A)
(so two depths give the tilt directly, and the constant -- which carries the)
(puck position, the puck diameter, the rod diameter and the tip centring --)
(cancels in the difference. The first plunge is 30 mm, deep enough that the)
(tip is already BELOW the puck, so the tip's own shape and squareness never)
(enter the measurement -- operator 2026-08-03.)
(Sequence, operator spec: touch top, touch bottom, CORRECT, touch bottom,)
(touch top -- if the spread did not shrink the math/sign is wrong, so ABORT)
(LOUDLY rather than iterate on a bad correction.)
(REQUIRES: rod stickout greater than the deep plunge -- 65 mm -- or the)
(shaft no longer spans the puck and nothing is touched.)
(Reports DELTA Y BEFORE and DELTA Y AFTER. Applies the A rotation; writes NO)
(zero and NO offsets -- setting A's zero is a separate, explicit step.)
(Results: #3050 = dY before, #3051 = dY after, #3052 = A correction applied.)
(#3069 accumulates every A correction -- it IS where A's true zero now sits on)
(the DRO, so cal_c_zero tilts +-45 about it instead of about the stale zero,)
(and every routine parks there. RECORD TO PARAMS is what finally banks it.)

(SCOPE NOTE: named parameters are LOCAL to the subroutine that assigns them,)
(so the wall-touch helper cannot see the caller's values. It is defined at)
(FILE level -- subroutine definitions do not nest -- takes its depth as a)
(positional argument, and reads the shared setup from GLOBAL _ca_ parameters)
(set by the caller. It returns the touch Y in the global #<_ca_ty>.)

(============================== main cycle =================================)
o<cal_a_zero> sub
  #<cx>    = #1        (setter centre X, work frame -- from #3045)
  #<cy>    = #2        (setter centre Y, work frame -- from #3046)
  #<top>   = #3        (setter top Z, work frame -- from #3047)

  #<d_top> = 30.0      (shallow plunge below the top, operator 2026-08-03)
  #<d_bot> = 65.0      (deep plunge below the top, operator 2026-08-03)

  o5 if [#<_metric> EQ 0]
    (abort, CAL A: switch to MM first)
  o5 endif
  o6 if [#<top> EQ 0 AND #<cx> EQ 0 AND #<cy> EQ 0]
    (abort, CAL A: no setter centre - run the centre calibration first)
  o6 endif

  (--- shared setup, GLOBAL so the file-level helper can read it -----------)
  #<_ca_cx>    = #<cx>
  #<_ca_cy>    = #<cy>
  #<_ca_top>   = #<top>
  #<_ca_stand> = 30.0  (Y standoff from centre: outside puck + rod radius)
  #<_ca_reach> = 28.0  (max inward probe travel from the standoff)
  #<_ca_fpr>   = 100.0 (probe feed, operator spec)
  #<_ca_fla>   = 10.0  (latch feed, operator spec)
  #<_ca_ftr>   = 500.0 (traverse)
  #<_ca_fck>   = 200.0 (protective descent)
  (1 mm is plenty. A probe that will not release inside it is an ELECTRICAL)
  (contact fault -- fix the contact, not the distance. Operator 2026-08-03.)
  #<_ca_back>  = 1.0
  (clearance is 5 mm for every cal routine and IS the zero pose, so there is)
  (no rise needed before moving sideways -- operator 2026-08-03)
  #<_ca_safe>  = 5.0
  #<_ca_side>  = -1    (approach from -Y, probe toward +Y; +1 mirrors it)

  M50 P0               (pin the feed override -- probes run at programmed feed)
  M64 P3               (puck UP)
  G4 P1.5

  (=== BEFORE: touch top, then bottom =====================================)
  o<ca_touch> call [#<d_top>] [1] [0]
  #<y_top_b> = #<_ca_ty>
  o<ca_touch> call [#<d_bot>] [0] [1]
  #<y_bot_b> = #<_ca_ty>
  #<dy_b> = [#<y_bot_b> - #<y_top_b>]
  #3050 = #<dy_b>
  (PRINT, CAL A BEFORE: y at -30 = #<y_top_b>, y at -65 = #<y_bot_b>, DELTA Y = #<dy_b>)

  (=== CORRECT: tilt = atan of dY over dZ, dZ = the depth difference =======)
  #<dz>   = [#<d_bot> - #<d_top>]
  (ATAN form copied from stock probe_corner_x_plus_edge_angle.ngc)
  #<tilt> = [ATAN [#<dy_b>] / [#<dz>]]
  #<corr> = [0 - #<tilt>]        (one sign; the recheck below proves it)
  #3052 = #<corr>
  (PRINT, CAL A: tilt #<tilt> deg over #<dz> mm - rotating A by #<corr> deg)

  o120 if [ABS[#<corr>] GT 5.0]
    G90
    G1 Z[#<top> + #<_ca_safe>] F[#<_ca_ftr>]
    M65 P3
    M50 P1
    (abort, CAL A: computed correction over 5 deg - refusing to swing the head that far on one measurement)
  o120 endif

  (rotate ONLY with the rod clear above the puck)
  G90
  G1 Z[#<top> + #<_ca_safe>] F[#<_ca_ftr>]
  G91
  G1 A#<corr> F600
  G90
  #3069 = [#3069 + #<corr>]

  (=== AFTER: bottom first, then top -- operator spec order ================)
  o<ca_touch> call [#<d_bot>] [1] [0]
  #<y_bot_a> = #<_ca_ty>
  o<ca_touch> call [#<d_top>] [0] [1]
  #<y_top_a> = #<_ca_ty>
  #<dy_a> = [#<y_bot_a> - #<y_top_a>]
  #3051 = #<dy_a>
  (PRINT, CAL A AFTER: y at -65 = #<y_bot_a>, y at -30 = #<y_top_a>, DELTA Y = #<dy_a>)

  (=== park at the zero pose, then verdict ================================)
  (clearance FIRST, then sideways -- the clearance height IS the zero pose,)
  (so arriving over centre at 5 mm up is the whole return.)
  G90
  G1 Z[#<top> + #<_ca_safe>] F[#<_ca_ftr>]
  G1 A#3069 C#3070 F600
  G1 X#<cx> Y#<cy> F[#<_ca_ftr>]
  G1 Z[#<top> + #<_ca_safe>] F[#<_ca_ftr>]
  M65 P3
  M50 P1

  o130 if [ABS[#<dy_a>] LT ABS[#<dy_b>]]
    (PRINT, CAL A OK: DELTA Y #<dy_b> -> #<dy_a> mm, A moved #<corr> deg. Sign is correct.)
    (DEBUG, CAL A: dY before #<dy_b>, after #<dy_a>, A corrected #<corr> deg)
  o130 else
    (DEBUG, CAL A FAILED: dY before #<dy_b>, after #<dy_a> - got WORSE. Flip side or the correction sign.)
    (abort, CAL A: correction made it WORSE - dY #<dy_b> then #<dy_a>. The math or the sign is wrong, flip the corr sign. Failing loudly by design.)
  o130 endif

o<cal_a_zero> endsub

M2 (end program)
